MiniMax DFlash strict accept patch for Lucebox public bdc706a.

What this does:
- Preserves strict mode as the shipped/default behavior: the original
  argmax-match / longest target-argmax-prefix rule remains active when the
  environment is unset or DFLASH_ACCEPT_MODE=strict.
- Retains eta and top-k as experimental, non-default provenance knobs from the
  banked typical/top-k investigation.
- Eta mode additionally accepts draft token t at position k when
  p_target(t) >= eta * max_j p_target(j).
- Top-k mode additionally accepts when draft token t is in the target top-k.
- When a draft token is accepted, the verifier token stream is still committed
  from the target-side verification path; the drafter only proposes candidates.

Knobs:
- DFLASH_ACCEPT_MODE=strict|eta|topk (default strict; env unset is strict)
- DFLASH_ACCEPT_ETA=<float> for eta mode
- DFLASH_ACCEPT_TOPK=<int> for top-k mode
- The dflash_llama serve-lucebox wrapper exposes --accept-mode, --accept-eta,
  and --accept-topk and maps experimental modes to the environment variables
  above. Strict mode leaves the accept environment unset.

Verifier-authoritative note:
- The target/verifier remains authoritative. Lossy modes only widen which draft
  proposals can be committed after target-side verification.

Provenance:
- Generated as a clean unified diff against github.com/Luce-Org/lucebox-hub
  at commit bdc706a.
- Touches only the DFlash target interface, shared weight compatibility structs,
  and Qwen/MiniMax DFlash backend.
- The shared struct additions are default-false/default-empty compatibility
  fields required because the public patch is cut from a later internal tree;
  they preserve stock public Qwen3.5 behavior and make the patch compile on
  public bdc706a.
- The new truncate_kv hook is a safe default (returns false) in the interface,
  so non-Qwen DFlashTarget implementers in the public tree remain concrete and
  compile; Qwen/MiniMax overrides it with the real logical KV trim used by this
  patch's no-replay verified-prefix commit path.

